      "answer": "The 2022 directive (AD 2022-03-07) is superseded by the 2024 directive (AD 2024-01-02). Regarding the 2020 directive (AD 2020-05-11), the context states it was \"partially superseded by AD 2022-03-07, fully superseded by this AD\" (this AD being 2024-01-02).\n\nFor current operators: the 2024 AD applies to Boeing 737-8 and 737-9 airplanes and requires MCAS Software v2.0 installation, revised FCOM procedures, and enhanced AOA sensor monitoring, effective February 15, 2024. Operators are legally required to comply with all applicable ADs under 14 CFR Part 39, and non-compliance renders the aircraft unairworthy for operation under FAA jurisdiction. The context does not state any further specific consequence of the 2022 directive's supersession beyond these facts.",
